    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass successfully. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nI fixed two issues in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Governance Module Export Issue** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n- **Problem**: The test file was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it wasn't exported from the module (only available in the default export).\n- **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` while preserving the default export.\n\n### 2. **Toxicity Metric Signature Mismatch** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n- **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function had a parameter named `bannedTerms`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metric functions with `(outputs, references)`. This caused references to be interpreted as banned terms, incorrectly flagging innocent strings as toxic.\n- **Fix**: Changed the function signature from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)` to match the interface expected by `runEvaluations`, while continuing to use the default banned terms internally.\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests pass across 8 test files  \n\u2705 All public exports remain available  \n\u2705 No test files were modified",
